&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Team description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Central Product Analytics team sits at the heart of how SumUp understands and improves the experience of millions of merchants using our products every day. This role owns the Engagement domain — covering merchant engagement, product activation, support responses, and navigation across the SuperApp and web dashboard — and is the primary analytics partner for the Engagement product team. It&#39;s a genuine opportunity to take full ownership of a domain, build the measurement foundations from the ground up, and shift the team from reactive reporting to proactive, insight-led decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define event taxonomies and measurement plans, implement and QA tracking (GA4), and make sure analytics is built into new product features from day one&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain scalable datasets in Snowflake — including funnels, customer behaviour models, and feature adoption metrics — and use them to generate insights that directly inform product decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and evaluate A/B tests: define success metrics, assess statistical validity, and communicate results clearly to product and engineering stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create and maintain intuitive dashboards and reusable query templates in Tableau that help teams answer their own questions without always needing an analyst&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with product managers to develop and map out KPI trees, identify measurement gaps, and improve the quality and accuracy of engagement tracking across the domain&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven experience as a Data or Product Analyst, with a strong track record of working with customer behaviour data and translating it into product decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced proficiency in SQL, including writing, optimising, and validating queries, building data models, and participating in code reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of data visualisation tools such as Tableau or Power BI, and experience with data warehousing platforms like Snowflake, Postgres, or Redshift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable designing and analysing end-to-end experiments, including A/B tests and feature flag rollouts, with a solid understanding of statistical validity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to communicate complex data findings clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, with strong written and verbal English skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office. This involves an office-first setup &lt;br&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced &lt;br&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success &lt;br&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education &lt;br&gt;💶 A corporate pension scheme where we match up to 20% of your contributions &lt;br&gt;🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days &lt;br&gt;🏋️ Numerous other benefits such as Urban Sports Club subsidy, Kita placement assistance, subsidised office lunches &lt;br&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service &lt;br&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 37 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;our diverse team&lt;/a&gt; of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our core values&lt;/a&gt; lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;careers website&lt;/a&gt;, and follow our journey on &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a class=&quot;text-primary underline cursor-pointer&quot; href=&quot;https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;TikTok&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to transform the way people shop and eat, connecting consumers, restaurants, shops, and riders to bring the neighbourhood to their door. We&#39;re redefining convenience by giving customers the ability to buy what they want, as they want it, when and where they want it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliveroo is a technology-driven company at the forefront of one of the world&#39;s most dynamic industries. We are a relatively small team making a very large impact, moving fast, valuing ownership, and tackling some of the most interesting challenges in global commerce. We&#39;re driven by innovation, autonomy, and the ambition to deliver exceptional experiences for our customers, partners, and riders alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own frontline operational performance across two closely linked parts of Deliveroo&#39;s customer support network: an in-house Global Escalations team of around 50 agents based across the UK and Georgia, and the outsourced network delivering support on our behalf through three BPO partners and three Shared Service Centres, circa 1,500 agents across multiple locations, including the team leads and ops managers embedded within those outsourced functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Escalations sits at the heart of Deliveroo&#39;s most critical customer moments. The team manages our most sensitive, high-risk, and high-impact contacts, including complaints escalated to the Executive team. As the leader directly accountable for this recovery-focused centre of excellence, you will ensure the team operates with exceptional skill, judgement, and empathy, protecting Deliveroo&#39;s reputation, driving improvement through root cause analysis, and embedding a culture of integrity and customer-first recovery across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the outsourced network, you own how performance is delivered day to day, working closely with the team leads and ops managers embedded in each BPO and Shared Service Centre, not just the vendor relationship at arm&#39;s length. You own the operational rigour needed to make the network the best in class, from an experience and consistency perspective, across every market it supports.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your key objective is to drive qualitative improvements to the customer experience, measured through CSAT, while balancing cost metrics like average handling time (AHT) and refund costs, rather than trading one off against the other. You will be the voice of Support to Deliveroo&#39;s market General Managers, taking full accountability for the Support experience in your markets, and you will partner closely with cross-functional Support &amp;amp; Operations teams, including Workforce Management, Training, Quality, and Policy, to drive initiatives that positively impact all three sides of the marketplace: customers, riders, and merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own frontline operational performance delivered through the in-house Global Escalations team (UK and Georgia) and the outsourced network (3 BPOs, 3 Shared Service Centres, circa 1,500 agents), including the team leads and ops managers within those outsourced functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the Global Escalations team directly, managing our most sensitive and reputation-critical contacts with judgement, empathy, and rigorous root cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive qualitative improvements to the customer experience, tracked through CSAT, while balancing cost metrics like AHT and refund costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of Support to Deliveroo market GMs, taking full accountability for the Support experience in your markets and representing their priorities back into the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Support &amp;amp; Operations cross-functional teams, including Workforce Management, Training, Quality, and Policy, to drive initiatives that improve the experience for customers, riders, and merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run performance frameworks that hold BPO and SSC team leads and ops managers accountable for quality, SLA adherence, and CSAT, fostering a culture of partnership rather than pure oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardise processes and playbooks across outsourced partners and sites where it drives consistency, while respecting genuine market and site-specific differences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and help bring down attrition and quality issues across the outsourced network, working with BPO and SSC leadership on the retention, engagement, and workforce planning changes needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Technology to shape the roadmap for customer support systems and channel strategy, identifying opportunities to enhance efficiency and automation across both in-house and outsourced teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with stakeholders across HR, Legal, and Policy to ensure service delivery evolves in line with business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive data-informed improvement through analysis of contact drivers, escalation themes, and customer sentiment, translating insight into action for both Global Escalations and the outsourced network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the function at relevant Weekly Business Reviews and senior forums, providing visibility on performance, risk, and recovery across both the in-house team and the outsourced network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the 24/7 Leadership Team on-call rota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape functional strategy and set OKRs for contact centre Support across Deliveroo markets, growing the remit from directing your own team to leading leaders, in line with DoorDash&#39;s Team Management career framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow and develop the managers and leaders within your network, including Team Leads inside Global Escalations and the team leads and ops managers at each BPO and Shared Service Centre, building the next generation of people leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our humble expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive contact centre, BPO, or shared service centre leadership experience in a fast-paced, consumer-facing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing outsourced or vendor relationships at scale, including the team lead and ops manager layer embedded within partner organisations, not just the commercial relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading escalations or complaint handling in a reputation-sensitive environment, with strong judgement and the ability to drive recovery from the most sensitive customer moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of bringing consistency and governance across multiple outsourced partners while respecting genuine local and market differences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing and reducing attrition while improving quality, in a large-scale, multi-site support operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven approach to balancing customer experience (CSAT) against cost metrics such as AHT and refund rate, without trading one off blindly against the other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a support or operations function to senior commercial stakeholders, such as General Managers or market leadership, taking full accountability for their experience of the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with cross-functional teams such as Workforce Management, Training, Quality, and Policy to drive improvements across a multi-sided marketplace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to influence senior leaders and work cross-functionally with Product, Legal, Policy, and People teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical ability, comfortable turning contact driver, escalation, and sentiment data into action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills, with experience building and developing a dispersed in-house team and driving performance indirectly through partner leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter mindset, a can-do attitude, and willingness to be hands-on in a fast-moving, multi-geography environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven strategic mindset with a track record of shaping and executing operational strategies across multiple markets and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep operational understanding, including customer service design, vendor management, and process optimisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to deliver results in high-volume, complex environments with multiple priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Product and Tech to drive tooling, system, and automation improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset focused on continuous improvement, customer advocacy, and operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate at a &#39;leads leaders&#39; level per DoorDash&#39;s Levels and Expectations framework (Team Management track): shaping strategy and OKRs beyond your own team, and developing managers who in turn develop their own teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meets the senior people-leadership bar DoorDash expects at this level: effectively leads a high-performing team, fosters a culture of belonging and engagement, and takes full accountability for the people outcomes of a large, dispersed organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/GoL541_xj9w&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at &lt;span class=&quot;_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9&quot; data-testid=&quot;smart-link-draggable-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;loader-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3&quot; href=&quot;https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-resolved-view&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-icon-and-title&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw&quot;&gt;Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Willst Du, dass Deine Arbeit eine echte Bedeutung &amp;amp; spürbare Auswirkung für uns als Gesellschaft hat? Hast Du Lust mit einem großartigen Team eine sichere, digitale Zukunft aufzubauen?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(222, 220, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;„In der Portfolio Unit Security &amp;amp; IT Solutions sorgen wir für die Sicherheit und Stabilität der IT-Systeme unserer Kunden. Gemeinsam übernehmen wir hier Verantwortung, liefern Produkte und professionellen Service, entwickeln und betreiben Lösungen und sorgen mit Freude dafür, dass die Welt ein Stück sicherer wird.&quot; - Christoph Wolf, Director PU Security &amp;amp; IT Solutions&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
